          %h2#Idea Idea
          %blockquote
            %p
              “Geometry is founded in mechanical practice, and is nothing but that part of universal mechanics which accurately proposes and demonstrates the art of measuring.” &amp;lbrack;
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Philosophi%C3%A6+naturalis+principia+mathematica"}> Newton (1687)
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Page:Newton%27s_Principia_(1846).djvu/73"} preface
          %p
            In its historical and etymological origins, “geometry” is the science of
            %em measuring the earth
            and here specifically of measuring
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distances"} distances
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/angles"} angles
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+geometry"} Euclidean geometry
            of the ancients and then eventually as the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry+of+curves+and+surfaces"} differential geometry of curves and surfaces
            due to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Carl+Friedrich+Gauss"} Gauss
            and others.
          %p
            But in modern
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematics"} mathematical
            jargon, the term
            %em geometry
            is used in much greater generality for the study of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spaces"} spaces
            equipped with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extra+structure"} extra
            “geometrical”
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
            of a large variety of sorts, foremost in the guise of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+geometry"} Riemannian geometry
            but subsuming also a wealth of variant notions of “geometries” which the ancient would not have recognized as such, for instance
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+geometry"} symplectic geometry
            and other (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+of+a+G-structure"}> torsion
            \-free)
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-structure"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                \-structured
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+manifolds"} differentiable manifolds
            (
            %em>
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+geometry"} Cartan geometry
            ), or (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+topos+theory"}> higher
            )
            = succeed "-theoretic" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            = succeed "\u201D)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+logic"} geometric logic
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+geometry"} functorial geometry
            famously including
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
            or
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
            but also more exotic variants such as
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+geometry"} arithmetic geometry
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absolute+geometry"} absolute geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+between+algebra+and+geometry"} duality between algebra and geometry
            to the extreme yields notions of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+geometry"} noncommutative geometry
            and/or
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+geometry"} derived geometry
            whose underlying “spaces” are only indirectly conceived as whatever it is that given (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+algebra"}> higher
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras"} algebras
            would see (measure!) if they are interpreted as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras+of+functions"} algebras of functions
            on a would-be space — which on the one hand is far remote from what Newton must have imagined geometry to be about, but on the other hand is quite in the spirit of geometry being about (maybe not space as such but)
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurement"} measuring
            space.
          %p
            Beware that bare
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            is sometimes regarded as a rudimentary kind of geometry (as reflected for instance in the common terminology
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
            for an operation that really is
            = succeed ")," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+realization"} topological realization
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            equipped with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extra+structure"} extra
            geometrical
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
          %p
